                "`fetch_corpus` returns the eight pinned row groups from the cache under `weights/belfort/` or the Hub at the "
                "pinned parquet-conversion revision — `pyarrow` reads the shard's footer and exactly those row groups over "
                "HTTPS range requests; every cached file is re-hashed and every fetched row group refused on any SHA-256 or "
                "byte-total mismatch — and `read_corpus` turns each row into a record: the line image (128 px tall, 145 to "
                "8,956 px wide) and its crowdsourced transcript with whitespace runs collapsed. `build_sample_dataset` draws a "
                "seeded split **by line image** (600 / 60 / 140). `validate_dataset` then checks every record against the "
                "contract, `check_split_disjoint` asserts no image (by decoded-pixel digest) is shared, and the training "
                "split's summary table is written to `outputs/{stem}_train.csv`.\n\n"
                "**What the split does and does not protect against.** No line image is in two splits. But the Belfort parquet "
                "has only two columns, `image` and `text` — no page, writer or register — so the split cannot keep a page's "
                "lines together: lines cut from one page can sit in training and in test, in the same hand. Nor would cutting "
                "the corpus into runs of consecutive lines help, because the shard is not in page order (neighbouring lines "
                "come from different years and registers: in the 800 lines, six of the eight pairs of year-bearing lines at "
                "most three rows apart name years more than two years apart, and the width of one line image predicts the "
                "next one's with a correlation of 0.02). The held-out rates in Section 8 are therefore a **same-collection "
                "estimate**: they measure lines from pages and hands the model may have trained on, and are likely optimistic "
                "for a new register or a new hand. A second, smaller overlap is textual: formulaic lines such as \"Le "
                "Conseil Municipal\" repeat across pages, so a few test transcripts also occur verbatim in training. The cell "
                "counts them (`transcript_overlap`), and Section 8 reports the rates with and without those lines.\n\n"
