        "## Glossary\n\n"
        "- **Task prompt token:** the token such as `<OCR>` or `<CAPTION>` that selects what Florence-2 generates.\n"
        "- **DaViT / BART:** the vision tower that turns the image into 577 visual tokens, and the encoder–decoder language "
        "model that reads them with the prompt and generates text.\n"
        "- **Beam search:** decoding that keeps the `num_beams` most likely partial outputs at each step and returns the "
        "best; deterministic for fixed weights, device and dtype. Greedy decoding is one beam.\n"
        "- **Levenshtein distance:** the minimum number of character (or word) insertions, deletions and substitutions that "
        "turn one string into another.\n"
        "- **CER / WER (micro):** total character (word) edits over total reference characters (words) across the split; "
        "**macro** is the mean of the per-line rates. Not capped at 1.0.\n"
        "- **Empty / constant-transcript baseline:** systems that never look at the image — predicting nothing, or one "
        "training transcript (the **medoid**, the line closest on average to the others) for every line.\n"
        "- **Teacher forcing:** during training the decoder is fed the correct previous tokens of the transcript, not its own "
        "predictions.\n"
        "- **Frozen encoder cache:** the encoder output for each training line, computed once without gradients and reused "
        "every epoch because nothing before the decoder is trained.\n"
        "- **Epoch / validation selection:** one pass over the training lines; the epoch kept is the one with the lowest "
        "validation CER (epoch 0 = the frozen model).\n"
        "- **Training / validation / test split:** lines used to train, to choose the epoch, and to report the final result "
        "once; split by line image, so no image is in two splits — but not by page (Section 4).\n"
        "- **Same-collection estimate:** a held-out score on data drawn from the same pages, hands and registers as the "
        "training data; usually optimistic for new sources.\n"
        "- **safetensors / adapter / reload parity:** a tensor file format that cannot run code when loaded; the saved "
        "trained tensors; and the check that a pipeline rebuilt from them and the pinned base gives the same transcripts.\n\n"
        "## Conclusion (your notes)\n\n"
        "Optional personal notes, not a required submission. Complete each sentence from your own run:\n\n"
        "- The task: from ___ to ___. On the test lines the empty baseline scored CER ___, the constant transcript ___, the "
